# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — instructions for coding agents

This project uses **Research Driven Development (RDD)**. The unit of work is the **experiment**; its artifact is the **experiment card**, one markdown file per experiment. These instructions apply to every coding agent working here.

{{ONE_LINE_PROJECT_DESCRIPTION}}

## Where things live

- `PLAN.md` governs: objectives, phases, gates, experiment matrix.
- Project map: `{{PROJECT_MAP_PATH}}` (orientation; never copy its tree here).
- Experiment status: `experiments/registry.json` (source of truth; dashboard `experiments/registry.html`).
- Cards: `experiments/<ID>/card.md`. Lab notebook: `notebook/NOTEBOOK.md` (`## Resume here` on top). Decisions: `decisions/`.

## Hard rules

- **One change per experiment.** Two changes = two cards.
- **Gates are declared on the card before launch.** Changing them later needs a dated decision entry.
- **Two human gates ⛔:** the researcher approves the card before any config, launcher or run; the researcher confirms the verdict before a gate counts as passed. The agent proposes; it never declares a gate passed.
- **No expensive or long compute without approval.** The smoke test passes locally first; cluster and paid runs are handed to the researcher (`{{COMPUTE_POLICY_PATH}}`).
- **Frozen artifacts never change:** {{FROZEN_LIST_OR_NONE}}. Verify with `scripts/check_frozen.py`; a replacement gets a new name and a decision.
- **Every run is logged** in the card's Runs table, failures and negative results included.
- **Data sensitivity:** {{DATA_SENSITIVITY_RULES}}. Never upload, print or commit: {{NEVER_LIST}}.
- **Domain constraints:** {{DOMAIN_SPECIFIC_CONSTRAINTS}}.

## Documents

- Human-facing documents are **markdown** from `{{HARNESS_DIR}}/skills/research-workflow/templates/docs/` — cards, plan, notebook, analysis reports (`reports/`), infra-specs (`specs/<module>/spec.md`), other notes. Format and budgets: `{{HARNESS_DIR}}/skills/research-workflow/doc-format.md`. Keep them short: Summary ≤ 3 sentences, one sentence per item, each fact once.
- Render for review with `{{RENDER_COMMAND}} <file.md>` (all: `{{RENDER_COMMAND}} --all`; Windows: `scripts/render.ps1`). The page `<file>.html` is generated — never edit it.
- The researcher reviews on the page and saves `<file>.feedback.md` (or pastes it). When asked to read the feedback: apply it to the markdown, re-render, delete the file. An approving file with no change/reject items is the researcher's gate decision.

## Commands

```bash
{{ENV_SETUP_COMMAND}}      # create/activate the environment
{{TEST_COMMAND}}           # tests (infrastructure)
{{SMOKE_TEST_COMMAND}}     # smallest run proving a job will not crash
{{SUBMIT_COMMAND}}         # how long jobs are launched
```

If a command is unknown, ask — never invent one.

## Skills

- `research-workflow` — the experiment loop: `{{HARNESS_DIR}}/skills/research-workflow/SKILL.md`. Classify first: infrastructure (infra-spec + tests) / experiment (card loop) / analysis (cited report).
- `bro` — re-explains the last answer, a file, an ID (`G1`, `Q2`, `E012_slug`) or a term in plain language, in a few lines.
- `closing` — before ending a session: brings registry, cards and notebook up to date and writes the `## Resume here` handoff.
- `rdd-update` — updates this harness from the research-onboarding-kit (installed version and files: `{{HARNESS_DIR}}/rdd-kit-manifest.json`).

